# Microchip PIC16F505 Configuration Word Definitions

# File Syntax:
# Each configuration register is given as:
# 
#     CWORD:<address>:<mask>:<default value>[:<name>[,<alias list>]]
# 
# for each CWORD the configuration settings are listed as
# 
#     CSETTING:<mask>:<name>[,<alias list>]:<description>
# 
# lastly for each CSETTING all possible values are listed as
# 
#     CVALUE:<value>:<name>[,<alias list>]:<description>
# 
# All numerical values are given in unqualified hex.  In terms of
# #pragma config, note the following correspondence:
# 
#    #pragma config CSETTING<name> = CVALUE<name>
# 
# The compiler may also emit a message when it detects certain programming.
# This behaviour is defined by the following record
# 
#     CMSG:<CSETTING name>=<CVALUE name>[,...]:<message number>
# 
# If the compiler encounters the given programming then it will emit the
# with the corresponding numnber.  Note that these records must appear last
# in the file.
# 
# Comments are also permitted.  Any line beginning with a '#'
# character will be treated as a comment.

CWORD:FFF:3F:FFF:CONFIG
CSETTING:7:OSC:Oscillator Selection bits
CVALUE:7:ExtRC_CLKOUTEN,_ExtRC_OSC_CLKOUTEN:External RC oscillator/CLKOUT function on RB4/OSC2/CLKOUT pin
CVALUE:6:ExtRC_RB4EN,_ExtRC_OSC_RB4EN:External RC oscillator/RB4 function on RB4/OSC2/CLKOUT pin
CVALUE:5:IntRC_CLKOUTEN,_IntRC_OSC_CLKOUTEN:Internal RC oscillator/CLKOUT function on RB4/OSC2/CLKOUT pin
CVALUE:4:IntRC_RB4EN,_IntRC_OSC_RB4EN:Internal RC oscillator/RB4 function on RB4/OSC2/CLKOUT pin
CVALUE:3:EC,_EC_RB4EN:EC oscillator/RB4 function on RB4/OSC2/CLKOUT pin
CVALUE:2:HS,_HS_OSC:HS oscillator
CVALUE:1:XT,_XT_OSC:XT oscillator
CVALUE:0:LP,_LP_OSC:LP oscillator
CSETTING:8:WDT:Watchdog Timer Enable bit
CVALUE:8:ON:WDT enabled
CVALUE:0:OFF:WDT disabled
CSETTING:10:CP:Code Protection bit
CVALUE:10:OFF:Code protection off
CVALUE:0:ON:Code protection on
CSETTING:20:MCLRE:RB3/MCLR Pin Function Select bit
CVALUE:20:ON:RB3/MCLR pin function is MCLR
CVALUE:0:OFF:GP3/MCLR pin function is digital input, MCLR internally tied to VDD
CWORD:400:FFF:FFF:IDLOC0
CWORD:401:FFF:FFF:IDLOC1
CWORD:402:FFF:FFF:IDLOC2
CWORD:403:FFF:FFF:IDLOC3
